<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    A stack buffer whose address escapes to a call is declared as long as the
    gap to the next frame object.  gcc and clang align a buffer of 16 bytes or
    more to 16, so the gap includes the padding below the next object, here the
    stack-protector guard slot at stack - 0x10: `char buf[64]` prints as
    `char [72]`.  Stage: P6 stack-frame layout (ScopeLocal::restructure), option
    arraysize off|on|calls.  Each function is decompiled with the option off,
    then on (float_text also at calls); the assertion counts span all passes.

    gcc 11 -O0 -fstack-protector-strong -fno-builtin -fno-pic, linked at
    0x401000; fgets, read, readlink, __snprintf_chk, memset, fmt_num, fill and use are stubs:

        int line_len(FILE *f)    { char buf[64];   if (!fgets(buf, sizeof buf, f)) return -1; return use(buf); }
        int link_len(char *p)    { char buf[4096]; ssize_t n = readlink(p, buf, sizeof buf - 1);
                                   if (n < 0) return -1; return use(buf) + (int)n; }
        int link_plus1(char *p)  { char buf[4097]; ssize_t n = readlink(p, buf, 4096);
                                   if (n < 0) return -1; buf[n] = 0; return use(buf); }
        int fortified(int v)     { char buf[256];  __snprintf_chk(buf, 200, 1, sizeof buf, "%d", v); return use(buf); }
        int float_text(long v)   { char buf[31];   fmt_num(buf, sizeof buf, v); return use(buf); }
        int short_read(FILE *f)  { char buf[64];   if (!fgets(buf, 16, f)) return -1; return use(buf); }
        int term_room(FILE *f)   { char buf[24];   if (!fgets(buf, sizeof buf - 1, f)) return -1; return use(buf); }
        int veto(FILE *f)        { char buf[24];   memset(buf, 0, 16); if (!fgets(buf, sizeof buf, f)) return -1;
                                   return use(buf); }
        int scan_back(FILE *f)   { char buf[64];   if (!fgets(buf, 60, f)) return 0; int i = 63;
                                   while (i >= 0 && buf[i] != '\n') i -= 1; return i; }
        int sum_n(int fd, int n) { unsigned char buf[96]; if (read(fd, buf, 90) < 0) return -1; int s = 0;
                                   for (int i = 0; i < n && i < 96; i++) s += buf[i]; return s; }

    scan_back and sum_n are compiled at -O2 (`__attribute__((optimize("O2")))`).

    Off (#2, #3, #5) is the bug: [72], [4104], [264].  On (#1, #4, #16, #6)
    ends each buffer at the count its library call states: fgets' 0x40;
    readlink's 0xfff, one short of a multiple of 16, keeps the terminator
    byte; readlink's 0x1000 plus the byte buf[n] = 0 can reach, since n is
    readlink's result; __snprintf_chk's destination object size 0x100, not
    its 200 length.
    Controls that keep the gap with the option on: float_text's 0x1f goes to
    the binary's own function, which only `calls` reads (#7, #8); short_read's
    0x10 is further short of the gap than alignment padding can be (#2);
    term_room's 0x17 is one byte short of the gap (#9).  veto's fgets states
    the whole 24-byte gap, so the shorter memset count does not decide (#9,
    #18, #21).  scan_back subscripts the buffer from 63 down and sum_n reads it
    up to index 95, so the fgets count 60 and the read count 90 do not bound
    what the C reads and both keep the gap (#2, #19, #20, #22); declared at the
    count, the printed subscripts would run past the array.  Every call keeps its arguments in every pass
    (#10-#15, #17, #18, #21).
-->
